diagnosis_text:
End-to-end connectivity between the OSPF-side host (pc0, 20.1.1.x) and the EIGRP-side host (pc12, 120.1.1.x) is healthy. Topology-wide tests show pc0 → pc12 and pc12 → pc0 pings succeed with 0% loss and ~1.3 ms RTT, confirming the cross-core path is up. The OSPF-to-EIGRP redistribution point (R11) is operating correctly: its FRR configuration explicitly redistributes OSPF into EIGRP and EIGRP into OSPF, and its routing table contains both OSPF-learned routes via 111.1.1.1 on eth1 (to the OSPF core) and EIGRP-learned routes via 112.1.1.2 on eth0 (toward the EIGRP domain). On the EIGRP side, R12’s configuration advertises 120.0.0.0/8 under EIGRP 100, ensuring pc12’s subnet is injected into the EIGRP domain and, via R11, into OSPF.

Mechanistically, with adjacencies up on R11 (OSPF on eth1, EIGRP on eth0) and mutual redistribution configured, reachability is expected, which matches the observed successful ICMP tests. Localization: R11 (eth1=B to OSPF; eth0=EE to EIGRP) is the redistribution ASBR; R12 (EIGRP) carries the 120.0.0.0/8 networks; R1 (OSPF) learns external routes from R11.

Root cause: No fault present at this time; the reported outage was likely transient or user-side.

Corrective fix: None required. If intermittent issues recur, monitor R11’s OSPF/EIGRP neighbor stability and interface flaps (eth1 and eth0) and review FRR logs for transient adjacency drops. === END ===